---
import Content from "../Content.astro";
import SectionHead from "../Section.astro";
import ProjectPubs from "../../layouts/ProjectPubs.astro";
import PubButton from "../buttons/PubButton.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import srGraphic from "../../assets/img/sr-graphic.jpg";
import cntl from "cntl";

const firstParagraphClasses = cntl`
  first-letter:text-8xl
  first-letter:font-semibold
  first-letter:mr-2
  first-letter:float-left
`;

const spaceClasses = cntl`mr-1`;
---

<div>
  <SectionHead
    title="Strontium Isotope Geochemistry & REEs"
    subtitle="Using fossil shark teeth as geochemical archives to calibrate Neogene chronology"
  />
  <Content>
    <p class={firstParagraphClasses}>
      Fossil shark teeth are remarkably durable and abundant in the fossil
      record, and they preserve geochemical signatures that record the chemistry
      of ancient seawater. My M.S. research focused on using strontium (Sr)
      isotope ratios and rare earth elements (REEs) preserved in fossil shark
      teeth as age proxies for Neogene fossil sites across Florida. Because
      marine Sr isotope ratios have changed predictably through geologic time,
      teeth that preserve primary geochemical signatures can be matched to a
      global Sr isotope curve to estimate the age of the deposit in which they
      were found.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2">
      This work demonstrated that marine strontium isotopes preserved in fossil
      shark teeth can calibrate Neogene land mammal evolution, providing
      chronological anchors for fossil sites that lack other reliable dating
      material. The approach has broad implications for improving the temporal
      resolution of Florida's rich Neogene fossil record and for calibrating
      biostratigraphic frameworks across the southeastern United States. I also
      investigated REE uptake patterns to assess diagenetic alteration and
      evaluate which specimens retain reliable primary geochemical signals.
    </p>
    <figure class="mt-6">
      <Image
        src={srGraphic}
        alt="Graphical abstract from Killingsworth et al. 2025 showing strontium isotopes in fossil shark teeth"
        width={900}
        class="rounded-xl w-full"
      />
      <figcaption class="text-xs text-porsche-950 dark:text-porsche-50 mt-2 pl-3 border-l-2 border-porsche-950 dark:border-porsche-50 leading-relaxed">
        Graphical abstract from <span class="italic">Killingsworth et al.</span>, 2025.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </Content>
  <div class="mt-4 mb-2 text-semibold text-lg">Publications:</div>
  <ProjectPubs author="Killingsworth et al.">
    <PubButton
      author="Killingsworth, S., MacFadden, B., Moran, S. M., Perez, V. J., Pirlo, J., & Ziegler, M."
      year="2025"
      title="Marine strontium isotopes preserved in fossil shark teeth calibrate Neogene land mammal evolution"
      doi="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.palaeo.2024.112698"
      pdfUrl="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.palaeo.2024.112698"
    />
  </ProjectPubs>
  <ProjectPubs author="MacFadden et al.">
    <PubButton
      author="MacFadden, B. J., Bohaska, D., Cone, L., Killingsworth, S. R., Zbinden, S. P., Moran, S. M., Perez, V. J."
      year="2024"
      title="Early Miocene land mammals and chronology of the Belgrade Formation, eastern North Carolina"
      doi="https://doi.org/10.1017/jpa.2024.68"
      pdfUrl="https://doi.org/10.1017/jpa.2024.68"
    />
  </ProjectPubs>
</div>